  "choice": "pack",
  "line": "It’s in the bag. Eight o’clock, sharp, and I’m not leaving you to eat dry pancakes again."
}

{
  "choice": "pocket_cart",
  "line": "That is not an archive, it's my voice. Keep it."
}

{
  "choice": "tear_carbon",
  "line": "Phil, that's my carbon copy, not yours, but since the Rialto's closing after tonight, I'm giving you the whole damn thing so you can frame it. Don't even look at me like I'm trying to save you."
}

{
  "choice": "take_case",
  "line": "Hold on, if you touch that case I’m filing a formal complaint. Rita, you’re buying the coffee, this is a hostile takeover."
}

{
  "choice": "booth",
  "line": "Eight o'clock, sharp. I'm not fighting the static."
}

{
  "choice": "keep_running",
  "line": "Leave the phone. It’s not going to change what’s in Pittsburgh."
}

{
  "choice": "draw_chair",
  "line": "So the phone stays, and the projector keeps burning a hole in the curtain. Fine. I need the seven o'clock slot to run my own segment, and I'm not letting the boss keep stamping his name on my work."
}

{
"choice":"public_too",
"line":"Seven o'clock is mine. Fix your own reel."
}

{
  "choice": "stay_put",
  "line": "Rita, if you're gonna fix the reel, do it over here. Don't make me walk back to the desk."
}

{
  "choice": "fit_foot",
  "line": "Come on, you stubborn piece of furniture. Phil's probably just reading the weather forecast to himself in the shed."
}

{
  "choice": "clear_space",
  "line": "Yeah, I'm doing this, so move your feet. Just load the tape and tell the boss it was an accident, because I'm not signing his name to my life."
}

{
  "choice": "set_mic",
  "line": "You want me to load it? Sure. I’ll just tell her it slipped out of the case, my bad."
}

{
  "choice": "public",
  "line": "Don't test it, it's live. Put your name on the line, or don't."
}

{
